  "description": "NCEI is the long-term archive for all NOAA coastal tide gauge data: 1-minute water level data from the NOAA/National Ocean Service (NOS) <a href='https://tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/products.html' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Center for Operational Oceanographic Products and Services (CO-OPS)<\/a> and high-resolution (10-second or 15-second) water level data from the <a href='https://www.tsunami.gov/' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Pacific Tsunami Warning Center (PTWC)<\/a> and the <a href='https://www.tsunami.gov/' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>National Tsunami Warning Center (NTWC)<\/a>.  Coastal tide gauge data also undergo quality control and harmonic analysis at NCEI. The raw data and products are discoverable via the <a href='https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/maps/hazards/?layers=6' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Map<\/a>, <a href='https://www.ngdc.noaa.gov/hazard/tide/' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Timelines<\/a>, and <a href='https://www.ngdc.noaa.gov/thredds/enhancedCatalogWaterlevel.html' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>THREDDS Data Server<\/a> links. Data are provided as netCDF and as gzipped comma-separated-values (CSV).<div><br /><\/div><div>Map legend:<\/div><div><img alt='Legend graphic for tsunami-capable tide stations' src='https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/maps/hazards/images/tidegauge_legend.png' /><br /><div><br /><\/div><div>Please contact haz.info@noaa.gov if you have questions.<\/div><div><br /><\/div><div><a href='https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/products/natural-hazards/tsunamis-earthquakes-volcanoes/tsunamis/tide-gauge-data' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>More information about tsunami-capable tide gauge data at NCEI<\/a><\/div><\/div>",
